# Firebase Configuration
# Copy this file to a secure location and set your actual API key
# DO NOT commit the actual API key to version control

# To use this configuration:
# 1. Create a file named 'firebase-config.js' (already created)
# 2. Set window.FIREBASE_API_KEY before loading the application
# 3. Or modify firebase-config.js to load from your secure configuration

# Example Firebase API Key (replace with your actual key):
# FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBqn10ZjuimbifYx_3813caY-s9boS7FKM

# Security Best Practices:
# - Store API keys in environment variables or secure vaults
# - Use Firebase App Check to restrict API key usage
# - Implement Firebase Security Rules to protect your database
# - Never commit actual API keys to version control